{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/underestimatedCount"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:STsE19underestimatedCountSivp::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"underestimatedCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["Swift"]}],"role":"symbol","title":"underestimatedCount","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence.underestimatedCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"underestimatedCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/underestimatedcount"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/underestimatedCount":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/underestimatedcount","title":"underestimatedCount","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"underestimatedCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/underestimatedCount","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"title":"MaximalCliques","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}]}}}